+| 1 | `main(["add", "-15.00", "groceries", "returned the blender"])` returns 0, appends a row with amount `-15.00`, prints `Added -$15.00 to groceries on <date>.` | `add` should accept them |
+| 2 | `add 0`, `add -0`, `add -0.00` still return 2 with `error:` on stderr | zero still rejected |
+| 3 | `list`, `top`, `summary` print refunds as `-$15.00` (also `-$1,200.50` and sub-dollar `-$0.50`, never `$-0.50` or `-$1.50` for 50 cents) | shown like `-$15.00` |
+| 4 | `summary` category and grand totals subtract refunds (e.g. 40.00 + -15.00 -> `$25.00`; a net-negative total prints `-$x.xx`) | totals subtract |
+| 5 | A refund written by `storage.append` round-trips through `storage.load` with identical amount (including `-0.50` -> -50 cents, `-15.00` -> -1500) | load back correctly |
+| 6 | `split` with a negative amount and `parse_amount("-5")` (default) still raise ValueError; recurring bills with negative amount still rejected | out of scope guard |
+| 7 | `top` still lists the largest positive expenses first; refunds sort last | `top` behaviour |
