+## Approach
+
+**Pattern reference**: `src/tally/money.py` + `tests/test_money.py`, `tests/test_cli.py` — imitate their style and fixtures.
+
+**Vital slice**: sign-aware money parsing/formatting in `money.py`, one shared formatter used by the four affected commands.
+**Cut list**:
+- `split`, `due` output formatting stays as is (positive only).
+- No "refund" CLI sugar.
+
+Plan:
+1. `money.parse_amount(text, allow_negative=False)`: accept a leading `-` only when `allow_negative` (also allow `-$15.00`). Default behaviour unchanged, so `split` and `recurring.py` still reject negatives.
+2. `money.to_plain`: sign-safe (format `abs`, prefix `-`).
+3. New `money.format_money(cents)` -> `-$1,200.50` style, sign-safe. Replace the repeated f-string in `cmd_add`, `cmd_list`, `cmd_summary` (both lines), `cmd_top`. Leave `cmd_split` and `cmd_due` alone. Check column alignment widths in `list`/`top` still hold.
+4. `models.Expense.__post_init__`: reject `amount == 0` only (non-int still rejected). Message: keep "amount must not be zero" wording; check existing tests that assert the old message and update only those.
+5. `models.new_expense` and `Expense.from_row` call `parse_amount(..., allow_negative=True)`.
+6. `reports.py` already sums signed values; leave it. `largest` stays as is.
+7. Update `add` help text to mention refunds (e.g. `-15.00`). Confirm argparse accepts `-15.00` as a positional.
